From: Poco F1 iOS port
Subject: [PATCH] Poco F1: tell the speaker driver that the amps protect the speakers

At full volume SweetSpeaker.driver's guard took up to 17.8 dB off a ringtone on the Poco F1: the sound crackled and
dropped to a low volume after a few seconds. The guard stands in for the speaker protection the Mi 8's TAS2557 lacks in
ROM mode. On the Poco F1 the TAS2559 runs TI's tuning program with the phone's calibration, as under Android, so the
protection is already there and the guard only got in the way.

kern.sweet_audio_amp_protects reads 1 on the Poco F1 and 0 on the Mi 8. The driver reads it once at start; an older
kernel without it leaves the driver's full guard on.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/dipper_audio.c b/bsd/dev/dipper_audio.c
index 147e8f5..63bc937 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/dipper_audio.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/dipper_audio.c
@@ -4183,6 +4183,23 @@ au_out_sysctl SYSCTL_HANDLER_ARGS
 SYSCTL_PROC(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_audio_out, CTLTYPE_INT | CTLFLAG_RW | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, 0, 0, au_out_sysctl, "I",
     "Mi 8 player output: 0 speaker, 1 earpiece (WCD9340 EAR; brings the path up) (3067)");
 
+/*
+ * kern.sweet_audio_amp_protects (3105), read-only: 1 where the amps protect the speakers themselves, so
+ * SweetSpeaker.driver leaves the power limiting to them. On the Poco F1 the boot job loads TI's tuning program with the
+ * phone's calibration into the TAS2559, whose DSP guards both speakers as it does under Android (without that program
+ * the amp scripts are never registered, so the amps stay off). The Mi 8's TAS2557 plays in ROM mode with no
+ * protection: there the driver's guard is the only one, and this reads 0.
+ */
+static int
+au_amp_protects_sysctl SYSCTL_HANDLER_ARGS
+{
+#pragma unused(oidp, arg1, arg2)
+	int v = sweet_board_beryllium() ? 1 : 0;
+	return SYSCTL_OUT(req, &v, sizeof(v));
+}
+SYSCTL_PROC(_kern, OID_AUTO, sweet_audio_amp_protects, CTLTYPE_INT | CTLFLAG_RD | CTLFLAG_LOCKED, 0, 0,
+    au_amp_protects_sysctl, "I", "1: the amps protect the speakers (Poco F1), the speaker driver's guard steps back (3105)");
+
 /* kern.sweet_ear_gain: (EAR PA index << 8) | (uint8_t)RX0 digital dB, applied at once when the earpiece is up */
 static int
 ear_gain_sysctl SYSCTL_HANDLER_ARGS
